Wrong (A): Assigning the entire cost to the longest-lived asset ignores the requirement to allocate based on relative FMV and would misstate depreciation for all other assets.
Wrong (B): Dividing equally among assets has no basis in the tax code and would distort each asset''s depreciable basis relative to its economic value.
