  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 1015(a), the donee''s basis is the donor''s adjusted basis ($5,000). Per Section 1015(d)(6), basis is increased by the portion of gift tax attributable to net appreciation: $800 × ($7,000 / $12,000) = $467. James''s basis is $5,000 + $467 = $5,467.
Wrong (A): $5,000 is the donor''s unadjusted basis and ignores the gift tax adjustment required by Section 1015(d)(6) when gift tax is paid on appreciated property.
Wrong (B): $5,800 incorrectly adds the full $800 gift tax to basis rather than only the portion attributable to net appreciation ($7,000 / $12,000).
Wrong (D): $12,000 is the FMV, but gifted property does not receive a step-up to FMV. That treatment applies only to inherited property under Section 1014.$EXPL$
