-- Q2559: Property Transactions: Basis [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): IRC Section 1014 governs property acquired from a decedent, providing a FMV basis (step-up or step-down) at the date of death. Section 1015 governs property acquired by gift, providing a carryover basis from the donor with a dual-basis rule for loss property.
Wrong (B): This reverses the two sections. Section 1014 applies to inherited property, not gifts; Section 1015 applies to gifts, not inheritances.
Wrong (C): Both sections apply to all types of property — real, personal, tangible, and intangible — not just real property.
Wrong (D): Neither section inherently provides a lower or higher basis. Section 1014 can step down basis, and Section 1015 carryover basis may exceed or be below FMV.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2559;

