  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 2032(a), when the executor elects the alternate valuation date, assets disposed of before the six-month alternate date are valued at the date of disposition. Since the stock was sold on August 15, 2026 — before the January 4, 2027 alternate date — its value on August 15 is used for estate tax and the heir''s basis under Section 1014(a).
Wrong (A): The date-of-death FMV would apply only if no alternate valuation election were made. The election overrides date-of-death valuation for assets disposed early.
Wrong (B): The decedent''s original cost basis is irrelevant for estate valuation; Section 2031 and Section 2032 use FMV, not historical cost.
