-- Q2574: Property Transactions: Gains/Losses [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Section 1250 recapture applies only to the excess of accelerated depreciation over straight-line depreciation. Since MACRS requires straight-line for real property (39-year nonresidential), there is typically no Section 1250 ordinary recapture. However, unrecaptured Section 1250 gain (total straight-line depreciation) is taxed at a maximum 25% rate.
Wrong (A): Section 1250 does not recapture all depreciation regardless of method; it targets only the excess over straight-line. Full recapture applies under Section 1245 for personal property.
Wrong (B): Limiting recapture to the year-of-sale depreciation has no basis in Section 1250; the entire excess over straight-line across all years is subject to recapture.
Wrong (C): There is no rule limiting recapture to only the first year''s depreciation; Section 1250 looks at cumulative excess depreciation over the entire holding period.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2574;

-- Q2575: Property Transactions: Gains/Losses [medium/L2]
