  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Paul''s total gain is $400,000 − $280,000 = $120,000. Unrecaptured Section 1250 gain equals the lesser of total gain ($120,000) or depreciation claimed ($120,000). Since both amounts are equal, the entire $120,000 gain is unrecaptured Section 1250 gain, taxed at a maximum 25% rate under Section 1(h)(1)(E).
Wrong (A): $0 would be correct only if no depreciation had been claimed, but Paul claimed $120,000 of straight-line depreciation that must be recaptured.
Wrong (B): $40,000 does not correspond to any valid calculation based on the given figures and understates the unrecaptured depreciation.
Wrong (C): $80,000 understates the unrecaptured gain; the full $120,000 of depreciation is subject to the 25% maximum rate since the total gain equals the depreciation claimed.$EXPL$
