-- Q2576: Property Transactions: Gains/Losses [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the Section 1231(c) five-year lookback rule, net Section 1231 gains are recharacterized as ordinary income to the extent of unrecaptured net Section 1231 losses from the five preceding tax years. Marcus has $15,000 of prior losses, so $15,000 is ordinary income and the remaining $25,000 is long-term capital gain.
Wrong (A): Treating the entire $40,000 as long-term capital gain ignores the lookback rule, which requires recapture of the $15,000 in prior ordinary losses.
Wrong (C): Treating the entire $40,000 as ordinary income overstates the recapture; only $15,000 of prior losses must be recaptured, not the full gain.
Wrong (D): This reverses the amounts — $15,000 should be ordinary (matching prior losses) and $25,000 should be capital gain, not the other way around.$EXPL$
