-- Q2578: Property Transactions: Gains/Losses [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 165(g), a loss from worthless securities is treated as a capital loss deemed to occur on the last day of the tax year (December 31, 2026). The holding period is measured to that deemed date, and if held more than one year, the loss is long-term.
Wrong (A): The loss is a capital loss, not an ordinary loss. Ordinary loss treatment under Section 165(g)(3) applies only to stock in an affiliated corporation meeting specific ownership requirements.
Wrong (C): The loss is deemed to occur on December 31 of the year the stock becomes worthless, not on the actual date of the bankruptcy filing. The holding period runs to December 31.
Wrong (D): Recognition does not require formal cancellation of the stock. Under Section 165(g), the loss is recognized in the year the stock becomes completely worthless.$EXPL$
