-- Q2579: Property Transactions: Gains/Losses [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 453, gain is recognized proportionally as payments are received. The gross profit percentage is ($100,000 − $60,000) / $100,000 = 40%. In year one, Ryan recognizes 40% × $30,000 = $12,000 of gain.
Wrong (A): $40,000 is the total gain on the sale but ignores the installment method, which spreads recognition over the collection period rather than recognizing all gain in year one.
Wrong (C): $30,000 is the total payment received, not the gain recognized. Only the gross profit percentage (40%) of each payment is taxable gain.
